// The main menu with a Ghoul2 model standing in it.
//
// This is ui/jkx_smoke.menu with one more item, and it is a separate file
// rather than an addition to that one because every other lane's frame is that
// one: the smoke shot is compared against itself in the depth pre-pass stage
// and counted for colours in three places, and a model in it would be a change
// to all of them for the sake of a lane none of them run.
//
// WHAT IT COVERS, which is new: Item_Model_Paint, its own refdef and its own
// light, ItemParse_asset_model_go, and a Ghoul2 model drawn by the menu system
// rather than by the game. The menu SYSTEM has always run here - the fixture's
// mainMenu is what the first screenshot of every run is a picture of - but
// every item in it until now was a coloured rectangle.
//
// WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER, and this is worth more than the coverage.
//
// It was written to measure the untextured lightsaber hilt: ui_shared writes
// MINUS ONE into mCustomSkin to mean "no custom skin", and the renderer used to
// read -1 as "there is one" and hand the default shader to every surface. The
// model below asks for no skin with an empty model_g2skin, which is the same
// branch of ItemParse_model_g2skin_go, so it looked like the right fixture.
//
// It is not. Mutation tested by putting the old renderer test back: the frame
// is identical, to the pixel, 24948 blue either way. So mCustomSkin is not -1
// by the time this model is drawn, and the most likely reason is order - the
// saber path calls ItemParse_asset_model_go and THEN writes the -1, while here
// the -1 is written during the parse and anything that rebuilds the item's
// Ghoul2 instance afterwards starts it at zero again.
//
// The lane stays, because what it does cover was uncovered. But it does not
// measure the hilt, and it is written down here rather than left to be inferred
// from the lane's name. What would measure it is a fixture sabers.cfg naming
// this model as a saberModel with no customSkin line, and a menu item that
// takes UI_UpdateSaberHilt - which is the only caller that writes the -1 after
// the model exists.
//
// The colour is still the right colour for both questions: jkx/glm_baked is
// pure blue and nothing else in this fixture draws blue, so "the model kept its
// own materials" is an equality rather than an impression.
{
menuDef
{
	name					"mainMenu"
	fullScreen				1
	rect					0 0 640 480
	visible					1
	style					WINDOW_STYLE_FILLED
	backcolor				0.2 0.2 0.6 1

	itemDef
	{
		name				smokebox
		rect				64 64 512 352
		background			"jkx/smoke"
		style				WINDOW_STYLE_FILLED
		backcolor			1 0.3 0.1 1
		forecolor			1 1 1 1
		visible				1
		decoration
	}

	// No model_rotationspeed, deliberately. Item_Model_Paint turns the model by
	// realTime divided by that number when it is set, and a picture that turns
	// on the clock cannot be compared with another run of the same binary.
	//
	// The bounds, and both lines are here for a reason that is measured rather
	// than understood.
	//
	// A Ghoul2 model carries no bounds - Item_Model_Paint says so - and what it
	// falls back to when all six numbers are zero decides how far away it puts
	// the camera. So these have to be given.
	//
	// model_g2mins does not parse. PC_ParseFloat does not take a leading minus,
	// the tokeniser hands back the punctuation and then the digits, and the log
	// says "Unknown item keyword '-16'" three times per run. That noise is
	// expected and is not worth removing, because removing the line changes the
	// picture: 24948 blue pixels with it and 263 without, measured twice each.
	// Why a line the parser rejects changes anything is not established, and
	// saying so here is better than a tidy file that quietly measures a tenth
	// as much. It is the next thing to look at in this lane.
	itemDef
	{
		name				g2model
		type				ITEM_TYPE_MODEL
		rect				200 120 240 240
		asset_model			"models/players/jkxmenu/model.glm"
		model_g2skin		""
		model_g2mins		-16 -16 -16
		model_g2maxs		16 16 16
		model_angle			90
		visible				1
		decoration
	}
}
}
